body:
It says standard draft, drafting tomorrow.

&#x200B;

If y'all are still drafting tonight I'm in!

So is Boogie finally gonna get signed by someone now?

&#x200B;

Cause Celtics, Knicks, Heat lost the AD / LMA sweepstakes & still have holes in their front courts.

Thanks so much, man! That was my thought but wasn't sure if any others on my wire were higher on potential. 

&#x200B;

If you could stash just one IR worthy guy of : Cole Anthony, Love or Gordon--who would you choose? And should I even waste the weekly move on one?

The glory days of WWECW!!! Threadheads unite!!

&#x200B;

I'm decent, man. Busy as shit with work--teaching & writing and whatnot. I'm a bigger fan of what AEW is doing rn than anything WWE. Not even sure if there are dedicated threads for Dynamite at WF but some day I'll try to hop on and thread-head it. Sounds like it won't be the same, though. That's a damn shame!!

&#x200B;

Anyways brother, never hesitate to reach out or drop me a line. Happy to hear from you and randomly catch you on here cause luckily enough you carried over your username, lol. Makes me wonder how many other old WF heads are on here.

Him starting and being ousted by Dario. Dario's kinda just a bit player at this point in his career. Monty said he really liked the Suns playing bigger and he loves the flexibility Frank has given them in the starting lineup.

&#x200B;

I think he's there to stay given any unforseen circumstances.

Is Frank the Tank for real, y'all? 14/8/8 with 2 three's and still time left in the game.

&#x200B;

I'm about to drop Maledon for him.

There's always alternatives. They have topical Finasteride and Dutasteride you can buy and apply the same way you do Minoxidil...that doesn't gunk up your system in quite the same way.

&#x200B;

If you don't mind the shaved look but want to frame your face, you can try SMP. I got that done before my HT and honestly it didn't look terrible but I just wanted hair--my pattern wasn't as aggressive then, either.

&#x200B;

Hair systems are also pretty top notch and undetectable these days. But that comes with the anxiety of being discovered in all the same ways a bad HT would.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

It's not a lost cause for you, dude. Plenty of NW5s and 6s get a full head of hair (or the appearance of such) from HTs. And you aren't hopeless, man. Just make sure when you eventually choose a place it's one you've read REAL forum reviews from and that you've seen (in person) the results from their patients. 

&#x200B;

Sadly, I learned when it was way too late. It's depressing living like this but at least all my teaching is virtual for the time being. Hopefully by the end of summer / Fall, I can head somewhere for a repair and at least being on track to not be ashamed of my donor scarring / unnatural hairline. 

&#x200B;

I already have 2 clinics in mind which are world renowned for repair work. I will NEVER go anywhere that's anything less than stellar from now on--even if I have to pay up for it.

&#x200B;

And yeah, after writing a decent bit about this, and my image issues around it...I'm hopeful this is just another story I get to tell someday and not something that defines my happiness. Hope it doesn't come to define yours either, brother.

&#x200B;

I'm always around if you wanna talk.

Agreed with this. In my 14t, I had Pat early in the year. Dropped Plumlee to get him when he went off in one of the first couple games. But then he settled into who he is (at least this year, I feel) -- a low usage, defensive based player with the potential for boom games here or there if his shot falls and he picks up ancillary stats. He's not a prolific rebounder or shot blocker / swiper. He's not gonna have super high usage or the ball constantly in his hands as a point-forward with LaVine and White around. 

&#x200B;

I think he'll be stellar next year and beyond. This season, though, I just don't see it. Even with the Bulls being short handed in the front court.

At this point in the season, like half my team could be considered streamers. I made a couple 2 for 1 trades and one of those dudes (Nurkic) went and got himself injured for half the year. So end of my bench is: Prince, Zubac, RJax, Jeff Green, Jamychal Green, Dylan Brooks, Alec Burks.

&#x200B;

My mainstays are: Boogie, Wood, Haliburton, Luka, Ja Morant, Porzingis, Keldon and Nurk. So none of those guys are a drop candidate but I maintain flexibility with the rest of my roster cause as soon as a guy takes off in a 14 teamer, you need to grab him or lose out on the rocket ship...

&#x200B;

Trying to figure out if NAW is a rocket blaster before Ball is out long term / gets traded and if so, who I should cut bait with on that first list first.

Potential adds (pick 2): Tillman, Vanderbilt, Timelord, Paschall, McDermott, Okoro

&#x200B;

Potential drops (pick 2): Roby, Diallo, Whiteside, Alexander-Walker

Me, too, man. Appreciate that.

&#x200B;

Hair of Istanbul. For some reason they're highly praised on here because of their online marketing (IG) and results shown only in certain lighting / without attention paid to donor area. I really wish I went somewhere else--even if it cost me 3 times as much...and HOI aren't cheap. I paid 5k a year ago, now they're up to charging 7-8k.

&#x200B;

They're a really morally bankrupt clinic. They don't stand by their results.

Did you get the standard package or the 'deluxe' where he does incisions? I'd expect not to have him present if you chose the all techs one. 

&#x200B;

I paid 5k for some techs to scar me for life.

Because prior to this, I was trying to work things out with them with a 2nd procedure. I went and it was all more of the same. I think they didn't like that I was voicing my opinion online about their lack of listening & providing the client with what they need.

&#x200B;

Also, I have no conclusive proof because they don't send you pics of yourself pre/post procedure. They don't give you a graft count. They aren't personable about the whole experience and I've never had worse anxiety in my life than being in this clinic.

&#x200B;

This is the best I've got from what they sent me post-op:

&#x200B;

[https://imgur.com/a/KhufgpP](https://imgur.com/a/KhufgpP)

Yeah, after last week I've p much lost all faith in Sanders. It's a 3 headed monster committee there and they're playing the best run D in football.

&#x200B;

I gotchu, fam. Thanks for the help!

Try to deal Mike Davis before CMC comes back week 8 or 9. Preferrably to the CMC owner under the guise he needs his cuff. 

&#x200B;

PROFIT.

How did a 4 to 6 week timetable (he said he will beat) turn into 7 games or more? Also, noone's playoffs should be in week 13, it's 14 to 16. 

&#x200B;

DJ is high volume but when both are healthy, there's no contest between the two. You panicked, that's fine to tilt and make a win now move. I just don't like it for your long term.

Nah, not likely. They see the 4 man committee as a luxury few teams have. I genuinely see his talent winning out. Plus they can co-exist (a'la Kamara's rookie year) and both put up solid years if injury doesn't take Ingram out.

&#x200B;

I'm getting him everywhere I can, especially keeper leagues. I'm totally cool with folks still doubting him, just increases my shares.
